---
module: requires_chain
func_id: list-requires-chain
---

***conformance tests***

# chain-deepest-first
`chain_top` requires `chain_middle`, which requires `chain_base`; the chain of `chain_top` is `chain_base`, `chain_middle`, `chain_top`, and each tree has `functional specs`.

# single-module
The chain of `chain_base` is `chain_base` alone.

# shared-ancestor-once
`chain_fork_top` requires [`chain_base`, `chain_middle`]; its chain is `chain_base`, `chain_middle`, `chain_fork_top`.

# nested-walk-keeps-exports
`shared_export_above` requires `shared_export_top`; its chain is `shared_export_base`, `shared_export_middle`, `shared_export_top`, `shared_export_above`.

***acceptance tests***

# invalid-ancestor
`invalid_ancestor_top` requires `invalid_ancestor_base`, whose functionality mentions the undefined ⟨UndefinedThing⟩; parsing the top module alone raises an error holding `Concept ⟨UndefinedThing⟩ is not defined`.
